<div class="sop-meta">
  <div><strong>Trigger</strong> Site is live, monthly plan active</div>
  <div><strong>Owner</strong> Whoever is on rotation that day</div>
  <div><strong>Time</strong> Highly variable; most updates &lt; 30 min</div>
  <div><strong>SLA</strong> Same business day on routine; &lt; 1 hour on emergencies</div>
</div>

<h2>Channels</h2>
<p>Three places client requests come in. All three reach the same email inbox.</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Content update form</strong> at <code>/content-update/</code> &middot; structured, easiest to act on. ~50% of requests.</li>
  <li><strong>Direct email</strong> &middot; ~35%. Often just "hey can you change my hours."</li>
  <li><strong>Phone or text</strong> &middot; ~15%. For things they want to talk through.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Triage</h2>
<p>Within 30 minutes of receiving a request, classify it.</p>

<h3>A. Routine content update (same business day)</h3>
<p>Phone number change, hours update, photo swap, typo fix, price change, new staff bio, new testimonial, FAQ edit, banner add/remove, holiday closure note. Most requests.</p>

<h3>B. New page or section (1-3 business days)</h3>
<p>New service page, new blog post (if client drafted), new region/area page, new FAQ block, new gallery section. Quote-able if exotic.</p>

<h3>C. New feature (quote first)</h3>
<p>Calculator, booking integration, video page, custom form, third-party embed, anything that requires JS or a service integration. Reply with a scope + estimate within 1 business day.</p>

<h3>D. Emergency (immediate)</h3>
<p>See <a href="/sop/emergencies/">phase 10</a>. Different SLA, different process.</p>

<h2>Routine update workflow</h2>

<ul class="sop-checklist">
  <li>Acknowledge receipt within 30 min during business hours. One-line "got it, on it today" is enough.</li>
  <li>Open the client's repo in your editor.</li>
  <li>Make the change. Follow existing patterns; don't refactor surrounding code.</li>
  <li>Run <code>npm run build</code> locally. Verify the change renders correctly.</li>
  <li>Spot-check Lighthouse if the change touches performance-sensitive surfaces (hero, fonts, JS).</li>
  <li>Commit with a clear message: <code>"Update {X} per client request"</code>.</li>
  <li>Push to main. Cloudflare deploys in 60 seconds.</li>
  <li>Verify live. Check the actual URL the change should appear on.</li>
  <li>Reply to the client confirming with a screenshot or URL.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Templates</h2>

<div class="sop-template">
  <div class="sop-template-label">Acknowledge receipt (immediate)</div>
<pre>Got it, {first_name}. Working on this today; you'll have confirmation
by EOD.

— J</pre>
</div>

<div class="sop-template">
  <div class="sop-template-label">Confirm complete</div>
<pre>Done. Changes are live at {url}.

If you see anything not quite right, reply and I'll adjust.

— J</pre>
</div>

<div class="sop-template">
  <div class="sop-template-label">Quote needed before starting</div>
<pre>Hi {first_name},

Want to scope this before I start, since it's a bit beyond the usual
content update.

WHAT YOU DESCRIBED: {their_request}
WHAT IT'D INVOLVE: {bullets, plain language}
ESTIMATE: {hours / fixed cost}
TIMELINE: {when it'd be ready}

If that works, reply "go" and I'll start tomorrow. If you want to scope
something narrower, let me know and I'll re-quote.

— J</pre>
</div>

<h2>Monthly hygiene</h2>
<p>Once a month per client, run a 15-minute check.</p>

<ul class="sop-checklist">
  <li>Lighthouse mobile + desktop on the homepage + 1-2 key service pages. Flag any regression below 95.</li>
  <li>Check Search Console for crawl errors, Core Web Vitals warnings, indexing issues.</li>
  <li>Verify form submissions are flowing (look for any dry spell &gt; 10 days; check Web3Forms dashboard).</li>
  <li>Check uptime monitor: any incidents in the last 30 days? Any flaps?</li>
  <li>Review Cloudflare analytics: traffic trend, top pages, top referrers.</li>
  <li>If anything regressed, either fix it or note it for the client's monthly check-in email.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Quarterly check-in</h2>
<p>Every 90 days, send each active client a short check-in email.</p>

<div class="sop-template">
  <div class="sop-template-label">Quarterly check-in</div>
<pre>Hi {first_name},

Q-check-in. Site's been live {months} now.

LAST 90 DAYS:
- Page views: {n}
- Top pages: {bullets}
- Form submissions: {n}
- Uptime: {pct}
- Lighthouse: {scores stable / improving / regressed}

ANYTHING I NOTICED:
{1-3 observations: a slow page, a broken external link, a service
section that's not getting traffic, a competitor doing something
interesting, etc.}

ANYTHING I'D RECOMMEND:
{1-2 things, no pressure}

If you want to talk through any of it, 20 min next week works.

— J</pre>
</div>

