<h2>Common maintenance issues</h2>

<div class="sop-callout sop-callout--warn">
  <strong>Client requests something that contradicts the agreement</strong>
  Polite firm: "That's outside the monthly plan; here's what it'd be." Refer to <code>/agreement/</code>. Don't absorb scope creep silently.
</div>

<div class="sop-callout sop-callout--warn">
  <strong>Lighthouse regressed below 95 after a content update</strong>
  Don't ignore. Diagnose: probably a heavy image they sent that wasn't optimized, or a third-party embed they asked us to add. Fix it before the next deploy.
</div>

<div class="sop-callout sop-callout--warn">
  <strong>Form submissions stopped arriving</strong>
  Check Web3Forms dashboard. Check that the access key is still valid. Check the recipient inbox isn't filtering them as spam (common after a long dry spell). Test with a fresh submission.
</div>

<div class="sop-callout">
  <strong>Client asks for a feature I have built before for another client</strong>
  Don't reuse code if there's any custom-to-the-client logic. Re-implement cleanly to fit their site's voice + structure.
</div>

<h2>Exit criteria</h2>
<p>Maintenance is the steady-state, not a phase that exits. The only "exit" is the client moving to phase 12 (offboarding).</p>
